KG42.register("clusters-2ec804ab1812103a3a64ad92",{"id":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v142-d-K004","paper":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility","label":"Capacity-constrained clearing and price-difference remuneration for a general spatial virtual link","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"Capacity-constrained clearing and price-difference remuneration for a general spatial virtual link","market_meaning":"Clearing jointly selects demand, supply, and spatial load shifting, taking into account service cost, computing capacity, and network feasibility; the consumer bears the charge at the hub price, and cleared virtual load shifting receives remuneration according to the sending-minus-receiving nodal price difference.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M04"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"Restricted to (2.29) and to the charging narrative in that section that uses nodal prices. The computing-capacity constraint and the virtual-link capacity apply jointly; the adjusted-price convention of the subsequent M06 is not transplanted into this cluster.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The spatial load-shifting quota that is feasible under computing resources directly constitutes the metering input to the price-difference remuneration, and the two chains jointly express the clearing and payment of this service; the missing domain and set definitions still impede mathematical closure.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R013","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Determines the spatial quota that includes virtual load-shifting cost and computing-capacity limits."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R014","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specifies the hub-load charge and the virtual load-shifting remuneration."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-J01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R013::x::var_d_j","v141-c-R013::x::var_delta_v"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::x::v141-c-R014-X001","v141-c-R014::x::v141-c-R014-X002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"rationale":"The same spatially cleared load and virtual flow enter the hub charge and the load-shifting remuneration."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K004-J02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R013","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R014","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R014::theta::v141-c-R014-T001","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C002","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"rationale":"The source marks the clearing price at the spatial nodal balance and immediately explains charging by the hub price and the nodal price difference; only the coupling of the existing clearing and payment functions is recorded."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O01","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::x::var_d_j","v141-c-R014::x::v141-c-R014-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"rationale":"The same consumer's nominal cleared load is used as the charging input in the payment chain; it is not equated with the net physical load after load shifting."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K004-O02","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R013::x::var_delta_v","v141-c-R014::x::v141-c-R014-X002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"rationale":"The same capacity-limited virtual flow separately takes the roles of clearing selection and payment metering."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The demand, supply, and phase-angle capacity sets are only cited and are not expanded in the current chain, and the directional physical flow also has no explicit independent nonnegative domain. Constraining only the difference of the two directional flows is not sufficient to constrain the common component in the cost term, and the current content cannot serve as an already closed, independently computable model.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::x::var_d_j","v141-c-R013::x::var_p_i","v141-c-R013::x::var_f_k","v141-c-R013::x::var_theta_n","v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the capacity sets and directional flow domains that M04 explicitly inherits, and then have C record their definitions and citation scope."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G02","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The R013-C003 wording describes the virtual flow as having the receiving side on the left-hand side of the balance, whereas the frozen formula and source (2.29b) place the sending virtual flow on the left-hand side. The wording is inconsistent with the mathematical direction.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::phi::v141-c-R013-C003","v141-c-R014::phi::v141-c-R014-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C subsequently distinguishes explicitly the load-migration direction from the position in the physical power balance and revises the narrative explicitly; D retains the original formula and the original text."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The virtual link, the load-shifting service, and the computing-capacity constraint have not become approved independent graph objects.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R013::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R014::V::settlement.payment"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e029","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-p-virtual-link","v141-b-g02-p-load-shifting-service","v141-b-g03-P2-computing-capacity-constraint"],"required_work":"Manually review the proposal; the existing internal quantities and constraints remain frozen."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K004-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"Evidence in this cluster remains unverified, and the clearing and remuneration interfaces have only experimental-candidate status.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R013","v141-c-R014"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e026","v141-b-g02-e029","v141-b-g02-e030","v141-b-g02-e031"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Independently verify the source's flow direction, domain, computing capacity, and price convention; it cannot be concluded from this cluster that the scientific content has passed review."}]},"rule_refs":["42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R013","42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R014"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-29875534ea059f1d","COMP-ebacec241379c91d"]});
